{
  "id": "behavioral-phenotype",
  "term": "behavioral phenotype",
  "definition": "A behavioral phenotype is the pattern of behavior that emerges from the interaction of underlying personal characteristics, compensatory cognitive processes, and biological or environmental risk factors. In this source, it refers especially to a maladaptive pattern that can appear when neurodevelopmental risk factors weaken compensation and make behavioral difficulties more evident.",
